    {
      "id": "UvwMO",
      "type": "ref",
      "ref": "ui:Z4xcv",
      "name": "Label · Sign in · Community",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -3100,
      "width": 13760,
      "theme": {
        "ui:mode": "light"
      },
      "descendants": {
        "ui:E87RGF": {
          "content": "Sign in · Community"
        },
        "ui:G8OhZ": {
          "content": "Draft"
        },
        "ui:SH1DB": {
          "content": "/auth/login · /auth/signup (open only) · /auth/forgot-password · /auth/reset-password?token= · invite link → /auth/login?invited=1 · /auth/set-password"
        },
        "ui:z4SKuT": {
          "content": "Self-hosted variant: GetCapabilities returns auth.methods = [password]. auth.signup = invite (default) shows the admin-invite hint; auth.signup = \"open\" shows \"Create an account\" (Open sign-up) and Sign up / Community / Default (name, email, password ≥ 8 → existing CreateUser RPC, then Create workspace B0Ywlx). No GitHub. ExchangeCredentials(username, password, two_factor_code?) fails with \"Invalid credentials\" or \"Invalid 2FA code\". 2FA step only when IDENTITY_TWO_FACTOR_AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED: client calls public SendVerificationCode(EMAIL), then retries with the code. Reset: SendResetPasswordCode emails DASHBOARD_RESET_PASSWORD_URL?token=…, ResetPassword sets the new one (always answer \"if an account exists…\"). Invite: new users get a 10-char one-time password + a link to /api/identity/accept-invite, which activates the membership and redirects to the app. Set password is shown right after sign-in while mustChangePassword is true and can't be skipped (flag planned in identity-auth-modes). GAPS: GetCapabilities RPC; accept-invite redirects to the bare app URL (needs ?invited=1 for the banner); the 2FA code is sent before the password is checked (needs a two-step exchange)."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x3SE9",
      "type": "ref",
      "ref": "ui:Z4xcv",
      "name": "Label · Workspaces",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -1600,
      "width": 9140,
      "theme": {
        "ui:mode": "light"
      },
      "descendants": {
        "ui:E87RGF": {
          "content": "Workspaces"
        },
        "ui:G8OhZ": {
          "content": "Draft"
        },
        "ui:SH1DB": {
          "content": "/ (index after sign-in) · New workspace → Sign in / Create workspace (B0Ywlx) · topbar switcher"
        },
        "ui:z4SKuT": {
          "content": "ListWorkspaces returns ref, name, owner {name, email}, createdAt (identity.proto Workspace); only ACTIVE memberships + owned workspaces are listed, so pending invites don't show. Role comes from the access token's access[].role (OWNER / ADMIN / MEMBER) matched by accessKeyId. CreateWorkspace takes a name only; members are invited later in Settings › Members. \"New workspace\" opens B0Ywlx (when the user already has workspaces: heading \"New workspace\" + Cancel back here). The switcher lives at the top of the sidebar under the logo (collapsed rail: initials-only 40×40 button) and opens this menu. GAPS: member count per workspace (ListWorkspaceMembers is workspace-scoped; needs memberCount on Workspace), last activity, pending invites for the signed-in user. Old UI hardcoded region NYC01."
        }
      }
    },
